<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Wix xmlns="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs">

  <Fragment>
    <!-- The entire staged publish tree, harvested wholesale. This replaces the vdproj's hand-maintained
         list of 24 files, which had drifted from what `dotnet publish` actually produces: it was missing
         Keysharp.png (Keyview prefers it over Keysharp.ico for its window icon) and it shipped
         assets\InstallerBanner.bmp, a Setup UI asset, into the application folder.

         Harvesting is only correct because the staged tree now contains exactly what should ship - see the
         payload cleanup in Directory.Build.props (no Release .pdb), Keysharp.csproj / Keyview.csproj
         (PreserveCompilationContext off, so no refs/ folder; Icon.icns is macOS-only). There is
         deliberately no Exclude list here: anything that should not ship must be kept out of the staged
         tree, so that the zip and the MSI cannot disagree again.

         Component GUIDs are generated from each file's target path and are therefore stable across
         releases as long as the layout is. Subdirectories (Scripts\, Lib\, runtimes\<rid>\native\) are
         created implicitly. -->
    <ComponentGroup Id="PayloadComponents" Directory="INSTALLFOLDER">
      <Files Include="$(PayloadDir)\**" />
    </ComponentGroup>
  </Fragment>

</Wix>
